    {
      "problem": "The first 30 seconds uses think before showing the concrete decision; simulated clarity is 2/5 for all three overview personas.",
      "change": "Introduce named objects, a goal and disturbance before abstraction; test only the words heard at that checkpoint."
    },
    {
      "problem": "The opening depicts a generic robot or file icon next to text about bananas/doors, rather than the actual objects.",
      "change": "Add fixed local banana, plate, lid, door, handle, gripper and token drawings; plan objects for task and decision steps; reveal the question before the final takeaway."
    },
    {
      "problem": "The narrative switches among banana/plate, a door, a pan and several metaphors without enough bridging.",
      "change": "Maintain the running example and explicitly connect each different paper experiment; keep useful humor attached to the same prediction and callback."
    },
    {
      "problem": "Some viewers can repeat the gist but cannot connect observations, predicates, operators and motion skills.",
      "change": "Blind viewer retelling, then separate source-informed editing against the intended question; add the missing causal step and recheck edited claims."
    },
    {
      "problem": "A request for optional algorithm details can be healthy curiosity, not a blocking comprehension failure.",
      "change": "Triage essential additions, later scenes, deep-dive details and untested limitations; preserve suspense and avoid overloading the opening."
    },
    {
      "problem": "The Local Attention overview says global attention can check the last position, then presents a formal inability without stating the changed model assumptions.",
      "change": "Require architecture restrictions, positional/output conventions and the scope of formal results before expressing limitations; never generalize a restricted theorem to all practical models."
    }
  ],
